{%- liquid
  assign s = section.settings

  comment
    A video picked in the editor wins over the pasted URL, so the file can be
    moved into Shopify's own hosting later without touching the section.
  endcomment
  assign poster = s.poster
  if s.video != blank and poster == blank
    assign poster = s.video.preview_image
  endif

  assign poster_mobile = s.poster_mobile
  if poster_mobile == blank
    assign poster_mobile = poster
  endif

  if s.video != blank
    assign video_alt = s.video.alt | default: s.video_alt
  else
    assign video_alt = s.video_alt
  endif

  comment
    The mobile cut is optional — most merchants only ever set the one video,
    so with nothing mobile-specific picked this falls straight back to it and
    the section behaves exactly as it did before this setting existed.
  endcomment
  assign has_video_mobile = false
  if s.video_mobile != blank or s.video_mobile_url != blank
    assign has_video_mobile = true
  endif

  assign ratio_mobile = s.ratio_mobile
  if ratio_mobile == 'same'
    assign ratio_mobile = s.ratio
  endif

  comment
    The quote goes to the script as data rather than as markup — it is painted
    into a canvas and handed to the GPU as a texture, so there is no element for
    it to live in. Newlines survive the attribute; the script splits on them.
  endcomment
  assign quote = s.type_text | strip | newline_to_br | strip_newlines | replace: '<br />', '&#10;'

  assign type_tracking = s.type_tracking | divided_by: 100.0
  assign type_leading = s.type_leading | divided_by: 100.0

  comment
    Phase boundaries, as fractions of the run: the quote is set by the first,
    has become film by the second, and starts coming apart at the third.
  endcomment
  assign phases = s.phase_set | divided_by: 100.0 | append: ','
  assign phases = s.phase_fill | divided_by: 100.0 | prepend: phases | append: ','
  assign phases = s.phase_dust | divided_by: 100.0 | prepend: phases
-%}

{{ 'video-parallax.css' | asset_url | stylesheet_tag }}
<script src="{{ 'video-parallax.js' | asset_url }}" defer="defer"></script>

<div
  class="vpx"
  data-vpx
  data-vpx-duration="{{ s.duration }}"
  data-vpx-push="{{ s.push }}"
  data-vpx-grain="{{ s.grain }}"
  data-vpx-grain-size="{{ s.grain_size }}"
  data-vpx-soft="{{ s.grain_soft }}"
  data-vpx-depth="{{ s.grain_depth }}"
  data-vpx-phases="{{ phases }}"
  data-vpx-autoplay="{{ s.autoplay }}"
  data-vpx-quote="{{ quote }}"
  data-vpx-type-size="{{ s.type_size }}"
  data-vpx-type-leading="{{ type_leading }}"
  data-vpx-type-weight="{{ s.type_weight }}"
  data-vpx-type-tracking="{{ type_tracking }}"
  data-vpx-type-family="{{ settings.type_header_font.family }}, {{ settings.type_header_font.fallback_families }}"
  data-vpx-bg="{{ s.color_background }}"
  data-vpx-ink="{{ s.type_color }}"
  style="
    --vpx-ratio: {{ s.ratio }};
    --vpx-ratio-mobile: {{ ratio_mobile }};
    --vpx-bg: {{ s.color_background }};
  "
  {{ section.shopify_attributes }}
>
  <div class="vpx__band" data-vpx-band>
    {%- comment -%}
      Hand-rolled rather than the `video_tag` filter: this is a texture source
      before it is a picture, so it needs `crossorigin` — without it the browser
      will not let a cross-origin frame be read into WebGL at all — and the
      script needs to own play and pause. Muted and inline are what make
      autoplay allowed at all on mobile.
    {%- endcomment -%}
    {%- if s.video != blank or s.video_url != blank -%}
      <video
        class="vpx__video"
        data-vpx-video
        crossorigin="anonymous"
        {% if poster != blank %}
          poster="{{ poster | image_url: width: 1600 }}"
        {% endif %}
        {% if s.autoplay %}
          autoplay
        {% endif %}
        {% if video_alt != blank %}
          aria-label="{{ video_alt | escape }}"
        {% endif %}
        muted
        loop
        playsinline
        preload="auto"
      >
        {%- comment -%}
          The mobile source has to come first: a browser picks the first
          <source> whose `media` matches, so listing it ahead of the
          unconditional desktop one is what lets the desktop source act as
          the fallback for every width the mobile query doesn't claim.
        {%- endcomment -%}
        {%- if has_video_mobile -%}
          {%- if s.video_mobile != blank -%}
            {%- for source in s.video_mobile.sources -%}
              {%- if source.format == 'mp4' -%}
                <source media="(max-width: 749px)" src="{{ source.url }}" type="{{ source.mime_type }}">
              {%- endif -%}
            {%- endfor -%}
          {%- else -%}
            <source media="(max-width: 749px)" src="{{ s.video_mobile_url }}" type="video/mp4">
          {%- endif -%}
        {%- endif -%}

        {%- if s.video != blank -%}
          {%- for source in s.video.sources -%}
            {%- if source.format == 'mp4' -%}
              <source src="{{ source.url }}" type="{{ source.mime_type }}">
            {%- endif -%}
          {%- endfor -%}
        {%- else -%}
          <source src="{{ s.video_url }}" type="video/mp4">
        {%- endif -%}
      </video>
      {%- if s.poster_mobile != blank -%}
        <script>
          (function () {
            var video = document.currentScript.previousElementSibling;
            if (video && window.matchMedia('(max-width: 749px)').matches) {
              video.poster = {{ poster_mobile | image_url: width: 1600 | json }};
            }
          })();
        </script>
      {%- endif -%}
    {%- else -%}
      {{ 'hero-apparel-1' | placeholder_svg_tag: 'vpx__video placeholder-svg' }}
    {%- endif -%}

    {%- comment -%}
      Where the whole sequence happens. Carries the quote for assistive tech,
      since the painted copy is pixels in a texture and reads as nothing.
    {%- endcomment -%}
    <canvas
      class="vpx__canvas"
      data-vpx-canvas
      role="img"
      aria-label="{{ s.type_text | strip | escape }}"
    ></canvas>
  </div>
</div>

{% schema %}
{
  "name": "Video Parallax",
  "tag": "section",
  "settings": [
    {
      "type": "header",
      "content": "Video"
    },
    {
      "type": "video",
      "id": "video",
      "label": "Video (desktop)",
      "info": "Overrides the URL below. Leave empty to use an externally hosted MP4."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "video_url",
      "label": "MP4 URL (desktop)",
      "default": "https://cdn.shopify.com/videos/c/o/v/d492a347093f4c8da210a74aece1224b.mp4"
    },
    {
      "type": "video",
      "id": "video_mobile",
      "label": "Video (mobile)",
      "info": "Optional — a differently-framed cut for the portrait crop below. The source ratio is a thin strip on a phone, so the same footage often needs its subject reframed. Falls back to the desktop video."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "video_mobile_url",
      "label": "MP4 URL (mobile)",
      "info": "Used only when no mobile video is picked above."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "video_alt",
      "label": "Video description",
      "info": "Read by screen readers. Used only with the MP4 URL."
    },
    {
      "type": "image_picker",
      "id": "poster",
      "label": "Poster image (desktop)",
      "info": "Shown until the first frame is decoded."
    },
    {
      "type": "image_picker",
      "id": "poster_mobile",
      "label": "Poster image (mobile)",
      "info": "Optional — falls back to the desktop poster above."
    },
    {
      "type": "checkbox",
      "id": "autoplay",
      "label": "Autoplay while on screen",
      "default": true,
      "info": "Always muted and looping. Ignored when the visitor has reduced motion on — they get controls instead."
    },
    {
      "type": "header",
      "content": "Shape"
    },
    {
      "type": "select",
      "id": "ratio",
      "label": "Aspect ratio",
      "options": [
        { "value": "1900 / 670", "label": "1900:670 (source)" },
        { "value": "21 / 9", "label": "21:9 (cinematic)" },
        { "value": "16 / 9", "label": "16:9" },
        { "value": "3 / 2", "label": "3:2" },
        { "value": "4 / 3", "label": "4:3" },
        { "value": "1 / 1", "label": "1:1" }
      ],
      "default": "1900 / 670",
      "info": "Match it to the file's own ratio and nothing is cropped."
    },
    {
      "type": "select",
      "id": "ratio_mobile",
      "label": "Aspect ratio on mobile",
      "options": [
        { "value": "same", "label": "Same as desktop" },
        { "value": "1900 / 670", "label": "1900:670 (source)" },
        { "value": "16 / 9", "label": "16:9" },
        { "value": "4 / 3", "label": "4:3" },
        { "value": "1 / 1", "label": "1:1" },
        { "value": "4 / 5", "label": "4:5" },
        { "value": "3 / 4", "label": "3:4" }
      ],
      "default": "4 / 5",
      "info": "The source ratio is a thin strip on a phone, and the pinned stage is a whole screen tall. A taller crop fills it."
    },
    {
      "type": "header",
      "content": "Playback"
    },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "duration",
      "label": "Length",
      "min": 2000,
      "max": 9800,
      "step": 200,
      "unit": "ms",
      "default": 5200,
      "info": "How long the whole sequence runs. It starts once the band is properly on screen, and plays once."
    },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "push",
      "label": "Push in",
      "min": 0,
      "max": 20,
      "step": 1,
      "unit": "%",
      "default": 6,
      "info": "How far the film is zoomed at the start, easing back to its true size as the sequence runs."
    },
    {
      "type": "header",
      "content": "Quote"
    },
    {
      "type": "textarea",
      "id": "type_text",
      "label": "Quote",
      "default": "Not anti-ageing.\nPro-longevity.",
      "info": "One line per line. Set in the theme's heading face, italic. Every counter and gap in it is a window onto the video, so a heavy face reads best."
    },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "type_size",
      "label": "Size",
      "min": 2,
      "max": 20,
      "step": 1,
      "unit": "%",
      "default": 5,
      "info": "Share of the band's width."
    },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "type_leading",
      "label": "Line height",
      "min": 80,
      "max": 180,
      "step": 5,
      "unit": "%",
      "default": 115
    },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "type_weight",
      "label": "Weight",
      "min": 300,
      "max": 900,
      "step": 100,
      "default": 500,
      "info": "Only weights the heading face actually ships will look right; the rest are synthesised."
    },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "type_tracking",
      "label": "Letter spacing",
      "min": -10,
      "max": 40,
      "step": 1,
      "unit": "%",
      "default": 0
    },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "grain_size",
      "label": "Dust fineness",
      "min": 200,
      "max": 2000,
      "step": 50,
      "default": 700,
      "info": "How many specks across the band. High is dust; low enough and they stop being specks and start being blocks."
    },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "grain_soft",
      "label": "Dust softness",
      "min": 0,
      "max": 95,
      "step": 5,
      "unit": "%",
      "default": 80,
      "info": "How far in from its rim each speck starts to fade. Low is hard little discs and reads as noise; high is soft and closer to a haze."
    },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "grain_depth",
      "label": "Dust depth",
      "min": 0,
      "max": 100,
      "step": 5,
      "unit": "%",
      "default": 70,
      "info": "How much the dust reads as a cloud with near and far sides rather than a flat field. Drives how fast the nearest specks stream past the slowest ones, how they are lit, and how much haze sits on the far ones. It clears as the dust settles."
    },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "grain",
      "label": "Film grain",
      "min": 0,
      "max": 100,
      "step": 5,
      "unit": "%",
      "default": 15,
      "info": "Film grain over the band while the sequence runs, reseeded every frame. It clears as the dust settles, so the finished picture is left clean."
    },
    {
      "type": "header",
      "content": "Phases"
    },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "phase_set",
      "label": "Quote is set by",
      "min": 3,
      "max": 40,
      "step": 1,
      "unit": "%",
      "default": 12,
      "info": "Point in the run where the last line has finished arriving."
    },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "phase_fill",
      "label": "Video has filled it by",
      "min": 10,
      "max": 70,
      "step": 1,
      "unit": "%",
      "default": 42
    },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "phase_dust",
      "label": "Dust starts at",
      "min": 20,
      "max": 90,
      "step": 1,
      "unit": "%",
      "default": 50,
      "info": "The gap between this and the one above is the hold — the quote sitting there, full of film, before it lets go."
    },
    {
      "type": "header",
      "content": "Colours"
    },
    {
      "type": "color",
      "id": "color_background",
      "label": "Background",
      "default": "#ffffff",
      "info": "The page the quote is set on, and the colour the grains eat away."
    },
    {
      "type": "color",
      "id": "type_color",
      "label": "Quote",
      "default": "#171717",
      "info": "The colour it holds at before the video comes through."
    }
  ],
  "presets": [
    {
      "name": "Video Parallax"
    }
  ]
}
{% endschema %}
